rule-name-prefix DQC

/** V31 Release **/

/**
Overview: The ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis is intended to be used in a consolidating schedule to disaggregate financial data for specific entities within a consolidated group. It should not be used to identify legal entities in the statement section of a filing. The LegalEntityAxis should be used instead to identify legal entities in the financial statements.

The SEC has observed issuers improperly using ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis to tag financial statements presented separately from the issuer's consolidated or combined financial statements. Examples include a trust that included the financial statements of an operating entity using ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis instead of LegalEntityAxis, and a trust with multiple series of units where each series' financial statements were tagged with ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis when each series should have been treated as a separate reporting entity using LegalEntityAxis.

Rule US.0245.10947 checks if any of the presentation networks in the statement section of the filing (identified using $STATEMENT_PRES_NETWORKS) include the ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis in their parent-child relationships. If found, the rule is not satisfied.

Approach:

Identify the presentation networks in the statement section of the filing. For each of these networks determine if the ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis is included as a concept in the network. If so, then the rule is not satisfied.
**/

ASSERT US.0245.10947 SATISFIED

$rule_id = (rule-name().split('.'))[rule-name().split('.').length];

/** DQCRT RULE **/
if not applicable_form(rule-name())
	skip
else

/** See the constants file that defines the variable $STATEMENT_PRES_NETWORKS **/

for $presNetwork in $STATEMENT_PRES_NETWORKS.sort
	$presNetwork.concept-names.contains(srt:ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis)

message
"The statement {$presNetwork.role.description} includes the axis ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis in its presentation relationships. The ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis is intended to be used in a consolidating schedule to disaggregate financial data for specific entities within a consolidated group. It should not be used to identify legal entities in the statement section of a filing.

The filer should use the LegalEntityAxis to identify legal entities in the statement section of the filing. If the ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis is being used with the member AffiliatedEntityMember to represent receivables from, or investments in, related parties, the RelatedAndNonrelatedPartiesAxis with the member AffiliatedEntityMember should be used instead.

Rule Element Id:{$rule_id}
Rule version: {$ruleVersion}"

severity error

effectiveDate $effective_dates[$rule_id]
